# Implementation Plan: Deploying IT Inventory to DeanOS

This plan outlines the steps to replace the current IT Inventory installation on the DeanOS server (`192.168.1.186`) with the updated "premium" version from the local workspace.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The deployment will involve restarting the `it-inventory` Docker container on the server. This will result in a brief downtime (approx. 30-60 seconds).
>
> [!WARNING]
> We will be syncing the `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/` directory on the server. A full backup will be created before any changes are applied.

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Local Synchronization

#### [TASK] Git Commit & Push
- Ensure all local changes in `C:\projects\it-inventory` are committed to the `main` branch.
- Push to GitHub origin (`evatechnosoft/My-Personal-Repository`).

---

### Phase 2: Server-Side Preparation

#### [TASK] Remote Backup
- SSH into DeanOS.
- Create a backup of the current project folder:
  `sudo cp -r /DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository /DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository_backup_$(date +%F_%T)`

---

### Phase 3: Deployment

#### [TASK] Pull & Rebuild
- Navigate to `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/` on the server.
- Force pull changes from GitHub:
  `git reset --hard origin/main`
  `git pull origin main`
- Rebuild and restart the container:
  `sudo docker compose up -d --build it-inventory`

## Open Questions

- Are there any specific database migrations we need to be aware of? (Currently, the app uses SQLite/SQLAlchemy with `Base.metadata.create_all`, which should handle additions automatically).
- Do you want me to keep the existing `data/` folder (database, etc.) or reset it? (Plan assumes keeping it).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- Check container logs on the server: `sudo docker logs it-inventory`
- Verify the container status: `sudo docker ps | grep it-inventory`

### Manual Verification
- Access the `it-inventory` UI via the browser (internal IP or Cloudflare tunnel).
- **CRITICAL**: Test the "Add New Device" and "Add Request" buttons to ensure the glassmorphism UI is fully functional and responsive (verified fix for the previous "unresponsive buttons" issue).
